CORE
main.py

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[exception.*uncaught exception: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
PLR §4.2.1: a reference to a name bound nowhere in the module raises
NameError. The frontend gates this on absence from the authoritative
all_bound_names set (computed by the AST server over every binding form),
so legitimately-bound names (tuple/for/with/except/comprehension targets)
are never misflagged.
